# Cancellation: its preconditions. The event itself uses api/trade_lifecycle_event.snippet, the checker task it creates
# api/trade_approval_rejection.snippet.

# ── Provisioning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@Given "^maker submit triggers a Cancellation event and task stored as '([^']*)'$"
    Given build json request from test data 'trade-cancellation' with trade id from stored variable 'createdTradeId' as user 'maker'
    When post to path '/trades/trigger-event'
    Then response status code is '200'
    And store response field 'data.results[0].checkerTaskId' as '$1'

@Given "^a '([^']*)' trade with pending cancellation is created and task stored as '([^']*)'$"
    Given a live '$1' trade is created via api
    And maker submit triggers a Cancellation event and task stored as '$2'

@Given "^a '([^']*)' trade with pending cancellation is created with trade stored as '([^']*)' and task stored as '([^']*)'$"
    Given a live '$1' trade is created via api with trade stored as '$2' and task stored as '$3'
    And build json request from test data 'trade-cancellation' with trade id from stored variable '$2' as user 'maker'
    When post to path '/trades/trigger-event'
    Then response status code is '200'
    And store response field 'data.results[0].checkerTaskId' as '$3'

@Given "^a live '([^']*)' trade with a pending Cancellation exists$"
    Given a '$1' trade with pending cancellation is created and task stored as 'createdTaskId'

@Given "^multiple live '([^']*)' trades have pending cancellation requests$"
    Given a '$1' trade with pending cancellation is created with trade stored as 'createdTradeId1' and task stored as 'createdTaskId1'
    And a '$1' trade with pending cancellation is created with trade stored as 'createdTradeId2' and task stored as 'createdTaskId2'
